    "title": "就 / 了: X就X or X了就X了 accepts a state or event",
    "subtitle": "Learn, understand, and use a Mandarin pattern.",
    "context": "Use the introduced pattern in a bounded sentence. Other wording may be valid Chinese; this task checks this pattern and these words.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk6-concession-frames-p02-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "就 / 了: X就X or X了就X了 accepts a state or event",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Repeat the state around the linking word to accept it, then dismiss the feared consequence. Acceptance of this result does not mean that improvement is unnecessary. This example accepts a state; the related event form adds the completion particle. Repeating a completed event with 了 acknowledges that it has happened and treats it as something to accept or set aside.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "这次说得不好就不好，没有什么不好意思的，下次再练习。",
                "pinyin": "zhè cì shuō de bù hǎo jiù bù hǎo ， méiyǒu shénme bùhǎoyìsi de ， xià cì zài liànxí 。",
                "meaning": "If you did not speak well this time, so be it. There is no need to feel embarrassed; practise again next time.",
                "audio": "29f237f573b2eeec3ae90ce65e1f9f0601d49883c6cd90fb34a627e1f9008bfd"
              },
              {
                "text": "忘了就忘了，别再想了。",
                "pinyin": "wàng le jiù wàng le ， bié zài xiǎng le 。",
                "meaning": "If you have forgotten it, let it go; do not keep dwelling on it.",
                "audio": "221f3a4d03b3924f4921e1f2ab033286e9c22690ebd8956fec8e3e5e9cc0afe2"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "title": "Words used in this pattern",
            "examples": [
